{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777387557,"nonce":"NY/b0RQKp6Wf+qIVwQXgZ5D2xww=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAu0T7A","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/97","origin":"github"},"title":"Operator-side diagnostics: monitor nodes + /diagnostics recorder on salmon","message":"## Summary\n\nOperator-side instrumentation is sparse compared to boat-side. During 2026-04-27 the operator had no real-time visibility into operator-router health, Starlink status, or — critically — when `/diagnostics` itself stopped flowing from the boat. Reactive recovery only (\"CAMP frozen → kill udp_bridge\"), no signal-driven response. **Class-prep priority for June 2026.**\n\n## Concrete actions\n\nThree bounded sub-tasks (could be split into separate PRs):\n\n1. **Run network/diag monitor nodes on salmon too**:\n   - `teltonika_monitor` pointing at the operator-side Teltonika router (192.168.13.1)\n   - `mikrotik_monitor` pointing at the operator-side MikroTik bridge dish\n   - `starlink_diagnostics` pointing at the operator-side Starlink (if present)\n   - `ping_monitor` for op-side targets (boat router, gabby, mercat, internet)\n   - Same nodes already running on gabby, just with operator-side configs\n\n2. **Salmon-side `/diagnostics` rosbag recorder** during deployments — small footprint, huge debug value. Operator-side wedge events become post-incident analyzable for the first time.\n\n3. **Operator launch file updates** (`operator_core_launch` in `unh_echoboats_project11/bizzyboat_project11`): bring up these monitors automatically alongside the existing operator stack. Pairs with [#28](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/28) (refactor operator launch files for cross-boat reuse).\n\n## Evidence — 2026-04-27\n\n[Dev log § \"Op-side diagnostics gap — class-prep priority\"](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/blob/jazzy/docs/logs/2026/2026-04-27_dev_logs.md):\n\n\u003e We have great visibility into boat-side state (gabby publishes diagnostics, mavros battery, all the cube_bathymetry and nav stuff) but **operator-side diagnostics are essentially missing** during the wedge / range events. Recovering the wedges was reactive (\"CAMP frozen → kill udp_bridge\"), not signal-driven.\n\nSpecifically blind to:\n\n- Operator router signal/quality to boat\n- Starlink stats (operator-side dish)\n- VPN tunnel state\n- Whether `/diagnostics` itself is flowing — when [`rolker/udp_bridge#10`](https://github.com/rolker/udp_bridge/issues/10) wedged, the annunciator silently kept showing the last-known OK state. The RTK loss at 19:15 EDT (NTRIP failed at 19:05, RTK degraded after the standard 10-minute coast) **had a properly-firing diagnostic on the boat side that never reached the operator UI** because the wedge had stalled the diagnostic stream.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] All four monitor node types run on salmon with operator-side configs\n- [ ] Salmon launches a `/diagnostics` recorder during deployments (start/stop alongside operator stack)\n- [ ] `operator_core_launch` brings these up automatically on next deployment\n- [ ] Verify on next deployment: operator-side `/diagnostics` recording captures wedge events with timestamps useful for post-incident analysis\n\n## Related\n\n- [`rolker/udp_bridge#10`](https://github.com/rolker/udp_bridge/issues/10) — udp_bridge wedge bug (the failure mode this instrumentation would have caught in real-time)\n- [`rolker/rqt_operator_tools`] — annunciator stale-stream indicator (separate UI work, complements this)\n- [#28](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/28) — operator launch files for cross-boat reuse\n\n## References\n\n- Triggering deployment: #94\n- 2026-04-27 dev log § \"Op-side diagnostics gap\"\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}